## Alternative: No Code Change Required

You can also workaround this issue without any code changes by setting the `id` field in your config to the full model ID:

```json
{
  "providers": {
    "groq": {
      "models": {
        "compound": {
          "id": "groq/compound",
          "name": "Groq Compound"
        },
        "compound-mini": {
          "id": "groq/compound-mini",
          "name": "Groq Compound Mini"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

This works because the existing code already supports the `id` field in model config:

```typescript
// Line ~854 in provider.ts
api: {
  id: model.id ?? existingModel?.api.id ?? modelID,
}
```

So users who don't want to wait for the code fix can just update their config to explicitly set the full model ID.

